<article class="env-lemma" id="0GA9">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GA9">Lemma <span data-tag="0GA9">51.22.3</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{F}$ be a coherent $\mathcal{O}_ X$-module. Then $\mathcal{F}$ is scheme theoretically supported on $Y_ c$ if and only if the canonical map $\mathcal{F} \to \mathcal{F}(c)$ is zero. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      This is true because $\mathcal{O}_ X \to \mathcal{O}_ X(1)$ vanishes exactly along $Y$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>